  m_Name: Scene12_FAQ_2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene12_FAQ_2
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: One ohm is the resistance of a conductor when a potential difference of one
    volt across it produces a current of one ampere through it. Our nichrome wire
    needs five volts for one ampere, so its resistance is five ohms.
